Every codec this image builds, and the one video display it has, are commented
out of the config baresip writes on a first run — so the phone negotiates G.711,
reports `Populated 0 video codecs` and has nowhere to put a picture, on a
machine carrying opus.so, vp8.so, vp9.so, avcodec.so and sdl.so.

The default is upstream's and is written for a build that may have none of
them: an uncommented `module opus.so` in a config on a machine without the
module is a start-up error. Here all five are built by this port and installed
beside it, so every line below is true wherever this config is written.

THE DISPLAY IS UNCOMMENTED AND THE CAMERA IS NOT, and the asymmetry is the
point: which screen a picture goes on is a property of the build, and which
camera it comes from is a choice. `x11` above it stays commented because this
image has no X server, and `fakevideo` below it is a null sink whose whole job
is to be chosen deliberately.

It is the GENERATED default and not a shipped file, because baresip writes
`~/.baresip/config` only when there is none — a person who deletes theirs gets
these modules back, and one who has edited theirs is not overwritten.

